### Page 1 of 1

```text
IAPPROVED
LBY Michael R. O’Donnell at 9:15 am, Jun 11
RESOLUTION NO.
ENTITLED:
“A RESOLUTION EXPRESSING THE INTEREST AND SUPPORT OF THE
GOVERNING BODY IN MOVING FORWARD WITH THE ‘HYATT PLACE
HOTEL AND CHEYENNE CENTER’ PROJECT.”
WHEREAS, the Governing Body held a work session on May 21, 2021, wherein a
presentation was made by ERES Capital and 307 Land Development for the “Hyatt Place Hotel
and Cheyenne Center” project (“Project”), a copy of which is attached hereto as Exhibit A and
incorporated by reference; and
WHEREAS, the Project holds significant potential benefit to the citizens of the City of
Cheyenne; and
WHEREAS, a Public-Private Partnership (P3) Structure is contemplated for the Project;
and
WHEREAS, significant due diligence needs to occur to determine the details of the
Project and its financing; and
WHEREAS, the Governing Body wishes to express it support for continuing to actively
investigate the possibility ofjoining the Public-Private Partnership.
NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE
CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, that the Governing Body expresses its interest and support
of the Project and the possibility ofjoining the Public-Private Partnership.
PRESENTED, READ, AND ADOPTED this
day of
. 2021.
Patrick Collins, Mayor
(SEAL)
Attest:
Kristina F. Jones, City Clerk
```
